{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Elohim saw the daughters of men.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'the sons of Elohim' are the rulers and the judges, because judges are called אלהים, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 22): ״אלהים לא תקלל״ — and we render it (in Targum) דיינא, 'a judge.' And Scripture says that those sons of the judges, whose duty it was to execute justice, were practicing violence against the daughters of men, whether by force or by consent. And 'they took them wives of all that they chose' — this was by force; and what it mentions, 'when the sons of Elohim came in unto the daughters of men and they bore them children' — this was by consent, for they would come upon them in the manner of harlotry, and the matter was not known until they bore them sons — 'and they were the mighty men that were of old.' That is to say, the people recognized that they were not the sons of ordinary men, but rather sons of these rulers and judges. And it says 'of all that they chose,' in the manner of what Scripture says (Isaiah 66): ״גם המה בחרו בדרכיהם ובשקוציהם נפשם חפצה״." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'the sons of Elohim' has already been explained above, and from there you will understand it, for all the matters of the work of Creation are doubled, and all is truth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Source cites Exodus 22 without a verse number; the citation אלהים לא תקלל corresponds to Exodus 22:27 in the Hebrew numbering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:41.729484425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}